"""Stanford source spec for the pre-2023 advising pass (gap 3, 2026-10-27), in the lab_sources.SOURCES format (see the
lab_sources.py docstring): lab_sources.py sets SOURCES['stanford'] from this module. Read by harvest_lab_sources.py stanford
(what to store) and records_labs.records_for('stanford') (how each stored page becomes records).

Why: Stanford Profiles list only CURRENT advisees and the SDR dissertation DOIs cover 2025-2027 degrees, so
hierarchy/stanford/students.json held few 2016-2022 students. Two kinds of source:
  pi-profile   Wayback captures of the PI's Stanford Profiles page (profiles.stanford.edu/<slug>), the first capture of each
               year 2016-2022 that the CDX index has (collapse=timestamp:4), accepted only when the page's <h1> is the PI
               (same family name and a shared full given name). Blocks 'Doctoral Dissertation Advisor (AC)', 'Doctoral
               Dissertation Co-Advisor (AC)' and 'Doctoral (Program)' -> phd; 'Postdoctoral Faculty Sponsor' and
               'Postdoctoral Research Mentor' -> other (postdocs). Readers, orals chairs / evaluators and master's /
               undergraduate program advisors are left out (as in the base sweep, st_profiles.ADV_KEEP). Each name is dated by
               its capture's year only (a current-advisee list says nothing about other years); a student listed on several
               yearly captures spans them. The anchor is the block text from its heading through the student's name, so the
               quote (anchor to the next PI family-name occurrence, normally the PI's own name in the publication list right
               after the block) states the relation. Captures already stored by the base sweep
               (claude-stanford-20261027/raw/captures.sqlite) were copied in unchanged (copied_from set). 'Doctoral
               Dissertation Advisor / Co-Advisor (NonAC)' -> phd as well. For the 30 'cs_related_scope_20261022' additions
               and the 3 newest PIs (Wager, Islam, Nair) every stored Profiles page 2016-2026 is used (live and Wayback),
               including those in hierarchy/cs-related-captures-stanford.sqlite, copied in unchanged by harvest_lab_sources.
  lab-roster / pi-homepage-style pages (kind lab-roster | colleague-page | dept-directory): hand-curated, see each note.
Generated by the gap-3 worker from its scratch tools (profile_harvest.py, gen_sources.py, write_module.py); edit by
regenerating, or append hand-curated sources to MANUAL.
"""

